# Files of the desktop distro which do not resolve, and why that is accepted.
#
# Anything unresolved which is not listed here fails 'make check'.

# the ICU integration of harfbuzz, which nothing in this distro links against.
# Resolving it means installing icu, 35 MB for a library no program here loads.

# firefox keeps its own libraries in /usr/lib/firefox and loads them itself,
# in the order listed in /usr/lib/firefox/dependentlibs.list. They are not on
# the loader's search path and are not meant to be: ldd cannot resolve them
# from outside, but firefox never asks the loader to find them by name.
#
# This is not the same kind of entry as the libharfbuzz-icu one that used to be
# here. That one hid a package the distro genuinely lacked, and was removed as
# soon as firefox needed icu for real. These four are present, next to the
# binary that loads them.
/usr/lib/firefox/libxul.so
/usr/lib/firefox/libmozavcodec.so
